# boru-project.jsonic — the PROSE half of the project knowledge graph:
# candidate facts about the boru-lang/boru repository drawn from its
# documentation. This is one of the two inputs kg/main.boru turns into
# kg/out/graph.json.
#
# THE OTHER HALF IS CODE, AND CODE WINS ON CODE FACTS. kg/gomod.boru
# reads go.work and every go.mod and emits the module inventory, the
# package inventory, and the directed depends_on edges, quoting the
# actual `use` and `require` lines as evidence. So those facts are NOT
# repeated here: this file no longer asserts `<module> part_of repo` or
# module-to-module edges, because prose could only say "eng builds on
# it" — undirected, and drifting the moment a go.mod changes.
#
# What stays here is what only prose knows: which document explains
# which module, what the language's design concepts are, and how the
# shipped artifacts relate.
#
# ONE COUPLING TO RESPECT. A candidate `entity` reference resolves only
# within its own bundle, so any module or package this file makes an
# assertion ABOUT must also be declared here — and its `key`, `type` and
# `label` must match kg/gomod.boru exactly (key `core-go`, type
# `SoftwareModule`, label `core/go module`; packages are
# `<path> package`), or the two declarations fingerprint to two
# different ids and silently split into two entities. The
# kg_module_without_code_evidence validation rule fails the build if
# that ever happens. Module ATTRIBUTES (path, go_module, unit) are owned
# by gomod.boru and deliberately absent below.
#
# Every assertion here quotes its supporting passage. When the
# documentation changes in a PR, update the affected entries and rebuild
# (see kg/README.md).
